1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,286
Meet Ray.

2
00:00:01,326 --> 00:00:02,124
He wakes up,

3
00:00:02,164 --> 00:00:03,613
and every other person

4
00:00:03,653 --> 00:00:04,964
on Earth is gone.

5
00:00:05,004 --> 00:00:06,641
"Finally, no traffic,"

6
00:00:06,681 --> 00:00:07,566
he says.

7
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:08,830
Soon the lights go out,

8
00:00:08,870 --> 00:00:09,894
because power plants

9
00:00:09,934 --> 00:00:10,745
shut themselves down

10
00:00:10,785 --> 00:00:12,522
when nobody runs them.

11
00:00:12,562 --> 00:00:13,573
Under New York,

12
00:00:13,613 --> 00:00:14,837
the subway pumps stop,

13
00:00:14,877 --> 00:00:16,113
and one estimate says

14
00:00:16,153 --> 00:00:16,964
the tunnels flood

15
00:00:17,004 --> 00:00:18,528
in about two days.

16
00:00:18,568 --> 00:00:19,792
Ray stocks up on cans,

17
00:00:19,832 --> 00:00:21,281
which keep their best quality

18
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:22,845
for two to five years.

19
00:00:22,885 --> 00:00:24,622
Food isn't his problem.

20
00:00:24,662 --> 00:00:25,973
Loneliness is.

21
00:00:26,013 --> 00:00:27,462
Being cut off from people

22
00:00:27,502 --> 00:00:29,164
raises the risk of early death

23
00:00:29,204 --> 00:00:30,654
about as much as smoking

24
00:00:30,694 --> 00:00:33,069
up to fifteen cigarettes a day.

25
00:00:33,109 --> 00:00:34,320
"Okay," Ray says,

26
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:35,671
"I miss traffic."

27
00:00:35,711 --> 00:00:37,587
Subscribe for more what-ifs.
